<p>This unusual poetic form made its first appearance in William Browne&#8217;s 1625 verse collection <a href="https://archive.org/details/brownebritanniaspastorals1625-01/page/80/mode/2up"><em>Britannia’s Pastorals</em></a>.</p>
<p>The text traces a single continuous intertwined line, involved with itself and never ending.</p>
